-- Lists Shale's C functions by how deeply their blocks nest, deepest first,
-- from the splitter the C recipes share (cookbook/c/items/, a Roc package).
-- The kernel's style guide calls more than 3 levels of indentation a smell,
-- so the line is depth 4 unless `min=` moves it.
--
--   shale cookbook:c/list_deep_nesting.shale             over c/, depth 4 or past
--   shale cookbook:c/list_deep_nesting.shale min=5
--   shale cookbook:c/list_deep_nesting.shale dir=c/host tests=1
--   shale cookbook:c/list_deep_nesting.shale self_test=1
--
-- It ranks functions to look at, never a rule or a gate: it fails on no
-- finding and exits 0 with them. Be aware of the opposite smell too:
-- one workhorse function that does a lot is sometimes better than complexity
-- scattered around the codebase.
--
-- How depth is counted: a function's own body is depth 1, and each block a
-- `{` opens inside it is one deeper, so `if (x) {` in the body makes depth 2.
-- Each body line is read through the splitter's masker (Mask.roc, which
-- does what c/check_discipline.shale's masker does), so a brace in a
-- string, a character literal or a comment is no brace. The dialect ends an
-- opening brace's line with it, so a line's braces are counted net: `} else
-- {` stays at its depth, and an initializer's `{1, 2}` on one line is no
-- level. A braceless `if (x) return y;`, on one line or two, is no level
-- either: depth is braces, not indentation. A body that shares its head's
-- line (`{ return x; }`) is depth 1. A body whose braces don't come back to
-- its own depth stops the run, naming it.
--
-- One line a function at `min` or past, deepest first:
--
--   path:line: name: depth N (at line L)
--
-- L the first line that reaches it. Then the summary: the functions read, how
-- many are at `min` or past, and how many there are at each depth. `tests=1`
-- measures each `TEST(` body too; by default tests are left out of both.
--
-- `self_test=1` runs it over cookbook/c/plants/list_deep_nesting/ and holds
-- every plant to its known depth and line, exactly: depths 3, 4 and 5,
-- braces in a string, a character literal and a comment, a braceless `if`,
-- an initializer's braces, the default `min`, and `tests=1`.
--
-- It is written in Roc, the app
-- cookbook/c/list_deep_nesting/list_deep_nesting.roc and the modules beside
-- it (Depth, the measure and the listing; SelfTest, the plants' check), over
-- the splitter package cookbook/c/items/, on Shale's Roc platform
-- (roc_platform/README.md); this file is its launcher. It hands every value
-- it is given to roc_platform/run.shale in the checkout this cookbook is in
-- (the `cookbook` mount's parent), which builds the Roc there (cached; the
-- first build after a change to C Shale compiles the platform's host, 25 to
-- 50 s) and runs the program rooted here, so `dir=` is this root's path. A
-- value the Roc reads no `Shale.arg!` of stops the run before anything is
-- built. `reads=inputs` builds and runs nothing, and prints the real path of
-- each file the program is built from (run.shale's header). It is built
-- with `opt=speed`, as map_file is: the masker reads a line a byte at a
-- time, which Roc's dev build does several times slower than the Shale
-- original's regular expressions; a stop in a speed build names the
-- platform's driver, not the Roc's line. Its goldens, the Shale original's
-- output on the plants, are held by
-- cookbook/c/list_deep_nesting/check_goldens.shale.
-- budget: programs=10 output_bytes=8000000

const SCRIPT = "cookbook/c/list_deep_nesting/list_deep_nesting.roc"
const CHECKOUT = dirname(dirname(real("cookbook:README.md")))
const HERE = real(".")

-- `self_test` is read here by name, as the cookbook's full tier finds the
-- recipes it runs `self_test=1` of. `arg_names()` is every value given; the
-- rest are read by a name made as the run goes, so Shale's own check cannot
-- see them: run.shale holds them to the script's reads.
const SELF_TEST = arg("self_test", "")
local values = {"script=" .. SCRIPT, "in=" .. HERE, "opt=speed"}
if SELF_TEST ~= "" then push(values, "self_test=" .. SELF_TEST) end
for name in arg_names() do
  if name ~= "self_test" then push(values, name .. "=" .. arg(name, "")) end
end
local r = run({"shale", "--root", CHECKOUT, CHECKOUT .. "/roc_platform/run.shale", "--args-stdin"}, {stdin = join(values, "\n") .. "\n", timeout_ms = 1800000, whole = 8000000})
print(trim_end(r.out))
if r.code ~= 0 then fail("list_deep_nesting: the Roc program stopped (exit " .. r.code .. ")") end
